* USENSB  1
Do we want to use NSB 1
* USEAFTERPULSING 0 0
Telescope type 0 Do we want to use Afterpulsing 0
* TRANSITTIMESPREAD 0 0
Telescope type 0 Transit time spread (RMS) [ns] = 0
* TELESCOPETRIGGERTYPE 0 3
Telescope type 0 will use Telescope-Trigger type : 3
* USETRIGGERSUBFIELDS 0 0
Telescope type 0 Will use patches : 0
* DISCPETOMVCONVERSION 0 4.6
Telescope type 0 The conversion factor at the input of the discriminator mV per pe (Amplitude)4.6
* DISCTHRESHOLD 0 -4.6
Telescope type 0 The Threshold of the discriminator in mV -4.6
* DISCWIDTH 0 100
Telescope type 0 The width of the discriminator output signal in ns 100
* DISCUSECFD 0 0
Telescope type 0 Do we use the CFD part of the discriminator: 0
* DISCUSERFBCIRCUIT 0 0
Telescope type 0 Do we use the RFB circuit: 0
* USEDISCCLIPPING 0 0
Telescope type 0 Signals will be clipped before summing 0
* GROUPMULTIPLICITY 0 1
Telescope type 0 The multiplicity requirement for a telescope trigger is 1
* USESUMTRIGGER 0 0
Telescope type 0 will use Sum trigger : 0
* TELMULTIPLICITY 1
The multiplicity requirement for an array trigger is 1
* TELNEXTNEIGHBOR 0
The array next neighbor requirement is 0
* ARRAYCOINCIDENCE 50
The coincidence window in ns on array level is 50
* FADCPETODCCONVERSION 0 24.1
Telescope type 0 The FADC conversion factor from DC counts amplitude  to PE is [dc/pe]: 24.1
* FADCDCTOMVCONVERSION 0 0.1
Telescope type 0 The conversion factor at the input of the FADC mV per dc (Amplitude) where the FADC response is linear. This number is used to pick the right pulse shape when assembling the trace. Note that for the trigger the high gain trace is used0.1
* FADCSAMPLINGWIDTH 0 10
Telescope type 0 The sampling time of the FADC in ns is: 10
* FADCOFFSETFROMTRIGGER 0 170
Telescope type 0  The offset between the beginning of the readout window from the trigger time in ns is: 170
* FADCSAMPLES 0 200
Telescope type 0 The number of FADC samples per recorded trace 200
* FADCDYNAMICRANGE 0 4096
Telescope type 0 The dynamic range of the FADC is: 4096
* FADCHILOGAINTHRESHOLD 0 10000
Telescope type 0  The lo gain is activated at dc : 10000
* FADCLOHIGHGAINRATIO 0 1
Telescope type 0 The gain ratio between the low gain channel /  the high gain channel (amplitude) 1
* FADCHIGHGAINPEDESTAL 0 500
Telescope type 0 The FADC high gain pedestal in dc is: 500
* FADCLOWGAINPEDESTAL 0 500
Telescope type 0 The FADC low gain pedestal in dc is: 500
* MAKEBIASCURVE 0
We make a bias curve 0
* BIASCURVERTELESCOPEID 0
the bias curve will be done for array telescope ID: 0
* BIASCURVETRIALS 1000
Trials that are done to make the bias curve 1000
* BIASCURVESTART -0.5
Start of the scan range for the bias curve in mV: -0.5
* BIASCURVESTOP -30
Stop of the scan range for the bias curve in mV: -30
* BIASCURVESTEP -1
Step in the scan of the discriminator values for the bias curve in mV: -1
* LOOPOVEREVENTS 1
We loop over events 1
* MINNUMPHOTONSREQUIRED 0 5
Telescope type 0 If more than 5 Cherenkov photons are in the focal plane of the camera the event is simulated
* WRITEVBF 1
Is a VBF file written?: 1
* SIMULATORNAME Jordan 
The Person executing the simulations: Jordan
* ATMOSPHERICMODEL 0
The atmospheric model used: 0
* DAYOFSIMULATEDEVENTS 2012-09-01
The simulated events will have a datum of: 2012-09-01
* NUMBERPEDESTALEVENTS 1
The number of pedestal events that will be simulated: 1
Note that this requires that you also set the write pedestal flag when calling CARE
* NUMBERPEDESTALEVENTSTOSTABILZE 1
The number of pedestal events that will be simulated to stabilize the discriminator: 1
* TLCFG 0  1 0 0.32   1.0  1.0  0.0
Telescope :0 SuperArrayID: 1 telType: 0 (id=0) sigma electronic noise: 0.32 relative gain: 1;  Winston Cone efficieny : 1 BlurSigma [mm]: 0
